//
// Does REWRITING a block compact it — here, on this box, with the loft that is installed?
//
// loft#730 reports that a store carries the 7/4 slack its vectors grew to, that compaction could not see
// it (the slack is INSIDE records, and the gate measured the space BETWEEN them), and that binding a
// store shed it: `nl-east.roads.store` 161 793 096 -> 81 271 776, content digest unchanged. Binding is
// gone (loft removed `store_persist_bind`, 2026-11); `store_persist_copy` now writes every image
// rebuilt and "sized to its content, with none of the growth slack the live store keeps". So a block a
// generator writes today should already be compact, and this measures whether that holds — on this
// box, with this binary (CLAUDE.md: anchor a finding to the binary).
//
// The smallest thing that answers it: load the block, count its records (so the read is a real one),
// write it back with `store_persist_copy`, and report the file size on both sides.
//
//   loft --native --lib lib tools/store_compact_probe.loft <block.store>
//
// ⚠ IT REWRITES THE FILE IT IS GIVEN. Point it at a COPY — or at a block you mean to compact, which is
// how `tools/cut-regions.sh` uses it. A block that fails to load is left untouched.
#cwd

use routing_kernel::(TTile, TRoad, TStep);

// ⚠ A BARE LOCAL, not a wrapper struct. This bound through `struct Block { roads: … }` until
// 2026-08-03, which means it COMPACTED AND CORRUPTED in one pass: loft#757 makes the image record the
// writing collection's root shape, so every other tool then fails to load the block it just shrank.
// Still true under `store_persist_copy` — a load into a wrapper is refused outright now.

fn main() {
  a: vector<text> = [];
  for x in arguments() { a += [x]; }
  path = a[0] ?? "";
  if path == "" { println("usage: store_compact_probe <block.store>  (rewrites it — use a copy)"); return; }

  before = file(path).size;
  b: hash<TTile[tkey]> = [];
  if !store_load(b, path) { println("#C FAIL could not load {path} — left untouched"); return; }
  // Read something real back: a "compaction" measured on a store nobody read is not a measurement.
  tiles = 0;
  roads = 0;
  for t in b { tiles += 1; roads += len(t.roads); }
  ok = store_persist_copy(b, path);
  after = file(path).size;
  println("#C write={ok} tiles={tiles} roads={roads}");
  println("#C bytes before={before} after={after}");
}
